I don't think we have got enough information from you to interpret the conditions when they are named a-f...

I take it pronoun use is the response not a predictor?

Also: if there are only 2 responses per subject per condition, then there must be *huge* inter-subject variation in order to support a subject random effect.  I'd think that plotting the subject-by-condition means would still be useful in these circumstances.

Roger


